.TH LINWIN 1 "2026-10-06" "linwin 1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linwin \- install Windows 10 as a dual-boot from Linux without a USB drive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linwin
.RB [ \-\-progress ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B linwin-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linwin
installs Windows 10 next to an existing Linux system without a USB stick or DVD.
It creates three partitions on the disk that holds the EFI system partition
(MSR, Windows, and a temporary FAT32 partition named WINSETUP that replaces the USB drive),
copies the Windows installer to WINSETUP, boots it once through a one-time UEFI entry
(BootNext), installs Windows (unattended if requested), then makes Linux the default
again and adds Windows to the boot loader menu.
.PP
Space is taken from unallocated disk space (any Linux filesystem; no existing partition
is modified), otherwise by shrinking a Btrfs root filesystem online, optionally inside LUKS.
.PP
.B linwin-gui
is a GTK 4 interface that runs the same commands.
.PP
Messages are in French.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Show whether this PC is supported, the available space, the boot loader and the drivers.
.TP
.B status
Print the complete state as JSON (used by the interface).
.TP
.BI "plan \-\-size " SIZE
Show the planned partitioning without changing anything (for example \fB100G\fR).
.TP
.BR iso " [" \-\-lang
.IR LANGUAGE ]
Download the Windows 10 22H2 ISO from Microsoft into ~/Downloads.
.TP
.BI "prepare \-\-size " SIZE
Create the MSR, Windows and WINSETUP partitions (root).
Options:
.B \-\-stage\-size
.IR SIZE ,
.B \-\-mode
.BR free | shrink ,
.BR \-\-yes ,
.B \-\-key\-stdin
(LUKS passphrase on standard input).
.TP
.BI "stage \-\-iso " FILE
Copy the installer to WINSETUP and add drivers (root). Options:
.B \-\-vmd\-driver
.IR DIRECTORY ,
.BR \-\-no\-net\-drivers ,
and for an unattended installation
.B \-\-edition
.BR Home | Pro | Education
.B \-\-user
.I NAME
.RB [ \-\-password\-stdin ].
.TP
.B boot
Start the Windows installer at the next reboot, once (root).
.TP
.BR finish " [" \-\-force ]
After Windows has finished installing: remove WINSETUP and the installer entries, make
Linux the default and add Windows to the boot loader menu (root). Runs automatically at boot
in unattended mode.
.TP
.B drivers
Copy network drivers to an already installed Windows (root).
.TP
.BR cancel " [" \-\-yes "] [" \-\-key\-stdin ]
Remove Windows at any step, even after installation, and give the space back (root).
.TP
.B install
Install a root-owned copy in /usr/local/lib/linwin (not needed when installed from a package).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
An x86-64 PC booted in 64-bit UEFI mode, a GPT disk with 512-byte sectors and a mounted
EFI system partition.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/linwin/state
State of the installation in progress
.RI ( state.done
once finished).
.TP
.I /var/lib/linwin/ptable-before.sfdisk
Backup of the partition table taken by
.BR prepare .
.TP
.I /run/linwin.log
Output of the running operation.
.SH NOTES
linwin downloads non-free software at the user's request: the Windows installation image,
the Intel RST driver from Intel and network drivers from the Microsoft Update Catalog.
Back up your data before changing the partition table.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR efibootmgr (8),
.BR sfdisk (8),
.BR wimlib\-imagex (1)
.PP
https://2deathadder.github.io/linwin/
.SH AUTHOR
2Deathadder
